>> title: Beef Stew, Instant Pot
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, dinner, one-pot, stew, potatoes, instant pot, pressure cooker
>> counters: Instant Pot
>> dish: beef-stew
>> kit: Instant Pot
>> aka: instant pot beef stew, pressure cooker beef stew, beef stew under pressure
>> pairs-with: dinner-rolls
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr 45 min
>> step.2: season, dry
>> step.3: brown 12 min, in two batches
>> step.4: soften, deglaze the base clean
>> step.5: 35 min high pressure, natural release 15 min
>> step.6: vegetables, 4 min, quick release
>> step.7: thicken, lid off

No flour on the beef: it settles on a sealed base and scorches, so the stew is thickened at the end instead. The potatoes go in after the meat, because thirty-five minutes turns them to soup.

Season @beef chuck{3%lb}(1.4 kg; cut in 2-in cubes) with @kosher salt{2%tsp}, @black pepper{1%tsp} and leave it dry.

Brown @&(~1)seasoned beef{} in @vegetable oil{2%Tbs} on sauté in an #Instant Pot{} for ~brown{12%min}, in two batches with room around every cube.

Soften @yellow onions{2%large}(chopped), @garlic{4%cloves}(minced), @tomato paste{1%Tbs} with @&(~1)browned beef{}, then pour in @dry red wine{1%cup}(240 mL) and scrape the base until nothing is stuck to it.

Pressure cook @&(~1)pot{} with @beef stock{2%cup}(475 mL), @thyme{4%sprigs} — half the stock the oven version takes, because a sealed pot gives back every drop it starts with — lid on and valve sealed, ~come to pressure{12%min}, then ~pressure cook{35%min} on high and ~natural release{15%min}, which is still cooking and is why thirty-five is enough.

Add @carrots{4%large}(cut in 2-in lengths), @Yukon Gold potatoes{2%lb}(900 g; quartered) to @&(~1)stew{}, seal it again for ~pressure cook{4%min} on high, and ~quick release{2%min} the moment it beeps.

Thicken @&(~1)stew{} on sauté with @cornstarch{2%Tbs}(16 g; slaked in 2 Tbs cold water) for ~thicken{8%min}, lid off, until it coats a spoon.
